Deleting a key while iterating over the dictionary changes its size. Iterate over a snapshot of the keys instead:

```python
for k in list(counts):
    if counts[k] == 0:
        del counts[k]
```

Or build a new dictionary:

```python
counts = {k: v for k, v in counts.items() if v != 0}
```

